{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-81737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ where $F(x,y)=(12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y})\\,i+(\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}})\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ g(y) & =\\frac{1}{y}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=\\frac{1}{y}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{1}{y}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "39c193f1cc3401bdeba1213ea0341a2c2400ea6be616a341f060e4cc2c682cd0"} {"question" "q-81737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=12{x}^{3}y-\\frac{x}{y}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=12{x}^{4}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}-\\frac{x}{y}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{y}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{1}{y}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81737" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{1}{y}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xy}\\,i+x{e}^{xy}\\,j+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{xy}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{e}^{xy} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(z) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z) \\\\ h(z) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "39c193f1cc3401bdeba1213ea0341a2c2400ea6be616a341f060e4cc2c682cd0"} {"question" "q-81741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y,z)=(x+y){e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{xy}+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)=y{e}^{xy}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3z)+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81741" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3z)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ where $F(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}\\text{ }i+(x{e}^{xy}+2y)\\text{ }j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+2y\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{xy}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy}+2y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{xy}+{g}^{′}(y) & =x{e}^{xy}+2y \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =2y \\\\ g(y) & ={y}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)={y}^{2}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{y}^{2}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81749" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "39c193f1cc3401bdeba1213ea0341a2c2400ea6be616a341f060e4cc2c682cd0"} {"question" "q-81749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y)=xy{e}^{xy}+y+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=x{e}^{xy}+2+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}+{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+xy+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{y}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-81749" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x,y)={e}^{xy}+{y}^{2}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-124733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\,i+2xy{z}^{3}\\,j+(3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z})\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-124733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2xy{z}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z) & =3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z} \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-124733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "39c193f1cc3401bdeba1213ea0341a2c2400ea6be616a341f060e4cc2c682cd0"} {"question" "q-124733" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-124733" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y,z)=xyz-y{e}^{z}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+yz-{e}^{z}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}+xz-{e}^{z}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y,z)={y}^{3}z-x{e}^{z}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-124733" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-132080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+(x{e}^{y}+2y)\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-132080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+2y\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+2y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}+{g}^{′}(y) & =x{e}^{y}+2y \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =2y \\\\ g(y) & ={y}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)={y}^{2}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}+C.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-132080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "39c193f1cc3401bdeba1213ea0341a2c2400ea6be616a341f060e4cc2c682cd0"} {"question" "q-132080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068604/state.json" "file_sha256" "202534ba6726bb083166bce8c40d3f4d284a5800b4ae3a87497ecd467c3fd1bc"} {"question" "q-132080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "f(x,y)=2y{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+y+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)=y{e}^{y}+x{y}^{2}+C"] ["math" "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y}+y+C"]] "category" "